From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenROAD <openroad@openroad.tools>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: avoid duplicate header paths in common_srcs and
 frontend_hdrs

frontend_hdrs used `strip_include_prefix = "src"`, which stages headers
under `bazel-out/.../external/sv-elab+/_virtual_includes/frontend_hdrs/`,
while common_srcs also included `src/*.h` at `external/sv-elab+/src/`.

When compiling `src/{builder,procedural,slang_frontend}.cc` in a consumer
that depends on both `common_srcs` and `frontend_hdrs`:
  - `#include "backend_builder.h"` resolves in the consumer package, whose
    `#include "slang_frontend.h"` resolves via `-isystem` to
    `_virtual_includes/frontend_hdrs/slang_frontend.h`.
  - `#include "slang_frontend.h"` directly from `src/*.cc` (or `statements.h`)
    resolves via same-directory lookup to `external/sv-elab+/src/slang_frontend.h`.

On Remote Execution (where `_virtual_includes` symlinks are materialized as
distinct files rather than symlinks to the same inode), `#pragma once` cannot
deduplicate the two paths and compilation fails with redefinition errors.

Expose `frontend_hdrs` via `includes = ["src"]` instead of
`strip_include_prefix = "src"` and keep `common_srcs` to `src/*.cc` so every
include resolves to a single path.
---
diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -75,14 +75,14 @@
 
 filegroup(
     name = "common_srcs",
-    srcs = glob(["src/*.cc", "src/*.h"]),
+    srcs = glob(["src/*.cc"]),
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
 
 cc_library(
     name = "frontend_hdrs",
     hdrs = glob(["src/*.h"]),
-    strip_include_prefix = "src",
+    includes = ["src"],
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
 
